ident Code Violation Criminal Activity Request Public Record Pavilion or Facility Rental Utility Service Recycle Bin Submit General Service Requests Police Records Request Contact Us News and Alerts Home News and Alerts RESCISSION OF PRECAUTIONARY BOIL WATER NOTICE FROM June 19th, 2026 Update as of June 21st, 2026. Due to an unplanned water service interruption on June 19th, 2026, the following area is affected: All of Carriage Cove, and the eastern part of Sunland Subdivision. All water is now safe to be used for drinking, cooking, making ice, brushing teeth, or washing dishes. Please contact the City of Sanford Information Line at (407) 688-5115 for a status report on your water. &times; Am I affected by this alert? PRECAUTIONARY BOIL WATER NOTICE FOR July 21st, 2026 Due to an unplanned water service interruption on July 21st, 2026, the following area is affected: 2570 Hartwell Ave #A - H 1309 Osceola Dr. 1311 Osceola Dr. 1312 Osceola Dr. 1310 Osceola Dr. As a result of this service interruption, residents in Sanford (please see map below to search for specific addresses) are advised to boil all water used for drinking, cooking, making ice, brushing teeth, or washing dishes vigorously for at least one (1) minute, or to use bottled water. This Precautionary Boil Water Notice will remain in effect until the issue has been resolved, and a bacteriological survey confirms that the water is safe to drink. For a status report on your water, please contact the City of Sanford Information Line at (407) 688-5115. We will continue to flush and sample your water until we are assured it is safe. Community News City of Sanford Moves to A Five-Day Public Service Schedule to Enhance Customer Access Reclaimed Water Service Interruption Notice Neighborhood Tree Trimming Schedule: Summer 2026 Utilities News and Projects Solid Waste Rate Increase Notification City of Sanford – Fire Hydrant Maintenance Notice 2nd Street Streetscape Improvement Project 2025 Public Works Projects Reclaimed Water Service Interruption Notice Neighborhood Tree Trimming Schedule: Summer 2026 Solid Waste Rate Increase Notification Parks & Recreation Update On Fort Mellon Park and Lake Carola Don’t Miss Our Summer Camps! Bingo at the Senior Center Public Art No posts found! Road Closures 2025 Parade of Lights – RCN Light Up Sanford – RCN Ace Cafe Biketober Fest Ace Cafe Biketober Fest – RCN City Commission City Manager’s Office City Clerk City Attorney Communications Community Relations Development Services Economic Development Finance Human Resources Fire Parks and Recreation Police Public Works & Utilities RESCISSION OF PRECAUTIONARY BOIL WATER NOTICE FROM July 15th 2026 Update as of July17th, 2026. Due to an unplanned water service interruption on June 15th, 2026, 200, 201, 205, 209, and 210 Tech Drive. All water is now safe to be used for drinking, cooking, making ice, brushing teeth, or washing dishes. Please contact the City of Sanford Information Line at (407) 688-5115 for a status report on your water. &times; PRECAUTIONARY BOIL WATER NOTICE FOR July 21st 2026 Due to an unplanned water service interruption on July 21th, 2026, the following area is affected: 2570 Hartwell Ave #A - H 1309 Osceola Dr. 1311 Osceola Dr. 1312 Osceola Dr. 1310 Osceola Dr. As a result of this service interruption, residents in Sanford (please see map below to search for specific addresses) are advised to boil all water used for drinking, cooking, making ice, brushing teeth, or washing dishes vigorously for at least one (1) minute, or to use bottled water. This Precautionary Boil Water Notice will remain in effect until the issue has been resolved, and a bacteriological survey confirms that the water is safe to drink. For a status report on your water, please contact the City of Sanford Information Line at (407) 688-5115. We will continue to flush and sample your water until we are assured it is safe. Water Quality Alerts and Service Updates Am I affected by this alert? The City of Sanford (City) is committed to providing safe drinking water to our customers. Sometimes, during planned system maintenance and construction or during unforeseen emergencies which could compromise water quality, it may be necessary to issue a precautionary (preventive) boil water notice to our customers. Some examples of unforeseen emergencies are broken water mains, loss of disinfection, treatment disruptions, hurricanes or floods, and losses of power or pressure at our facilities/water distribution system. General Boil Water Notice Information: If your area is under a boil water notice, you should boil all water used for drinking, cooking, making ice, brushing teeth, or washing fruits/vegetables and dishes prior to use. Heat the water to a constant, rolling boil for at least one (1) minute, or use bottled water. The water is safe for bathing, laundering, and other non-consumptive uses. Do not add bleach, chlorine, or any other substance, as a disinfectant to water in an effort to make it drinkable, as this may be extremely hazardous to your health. The most effective means to insure your safety is to boil water. The boil water notice will usually remain in effect for at least two (2) days while water samples are collected in the field and analyzed in the lab by a third party company. Customers should follow boil water procedures until the City notifies them thru the Boil Water Alert Information Line and the City’s website that the boil water notice is lifted and the water is safe for consumption. The City uses Alert Seminole to notify customers of boil water notices and rescission (lifting) of the notice if large areas of the City are affected – please sign up for Alert Seminole HERE . After your water service is resumed, it is advised that residents open their faucets for a few minutes to clear their water lines. Do not use the water until the water is running clear. You can call the Boil Water Alert Information Line at (407) 688-5115 for information on the status of a boil water notice. Prepare Seminole The City of Sanford partners with Seminole County and Alert Seminole on a variety of topics including notifying our residents about boil water notices and other safety concerns. Seminole County residents are encouraged to register for emergency alerts through Alert Seminole, Seminole County’s emergency notification and warning system. Residents can sign up to receive emergency alerts via text, e-mail, or voice call about a variety of potential public safety and environmental hazards, including: – Boil water notices and other safety concerns – Significant weather events, including hurricanes, tornadoes and severe thunderstorms – Evacuations – Shelter-in-place orders – Emergency shelter information – Highly disruptive road closures The City of Sanford Utility Department uses this tool to target messages to customers who may be impacted by Utility incidents, including storm related issues affecting residents. Register today. www.alertseminole.org Stay Connected, Stay Informed with the City of Sanford by following our social media. Connect with us on Nextdoor as well, and subscribe to our podcast – Sanford Say s and Youtube channel . Home Jobs Online Payments Contact Us Employee Email Accessibility Connect With Us facebook-square instagram youtube home linkedin twitter 300 N Park Ave Sanford FL, 32771 Opening Hours: Mon – Thur: 7:00 am – 5:30 pm Fri: 8:00 am – 1:00 pm Most Requested Events Calendar Special Event Application Rental Opportunities Water Service Building Permits Emergency Management Public Records Request Phone: 407.688.5000 Explore Parks and Trails Events Citizens Academy Community Center Sanford Airport Authority Stay Connected City of Sanford, FL | The Friendly City",
