            "text": "Water & Sewer Utilities | Sanford, FL Skip to main content Call: 407.688.5000 Open Hours: Mon - Thur 7:00 am - 5:30 pm & Fri 8:00 am - 1:00 pm Events Utility Payments Jobs News and Alerts Government Mayor & City Commission Mayor’s Youth Council City Manager’s Office Performance and Progress City Clerk City Commission Meetings Public Records Request Boards and Committees Communications Office Citizens Academy Connect with Sanford Connect Speakers Bureau Departments Organization Chart Community Relations Community Development Block Grant (CDBG) My Brother’s Keeper Development Services Planning Division Building Division Code Enforcement Lien Inquiry Procedures Economic Development Business Resources CRA (Community Redevelopment Agency) Finance Purchasing Division Human Resources Fire Contact Information Employment Public Services and Safety Information Fire Prevention Sanford Firefighters’ Retirement System Parks & Recreation Adopt-a-Programs Aquatic Center Parks Afterschool Programs, Youth Sports, Summer & Specialty Camps Adult Programs Senior Center and Programs Rental Facilities Museum Police Crime Prevention Records FAQs and Resources Public Works & Utilities Solid Waste and Recycling Water & Sewer Utilities Public Art City Attorney Residents Resident Guide Maps of Sanford Emergency Management Utility Services Building Permits Free Trolley Service Mayfair Country Club Marina & Marina Day Slips Community Survey Business Planning Division Economic Development Permits Special Events Business Tax Utilities Business Resources Visitors About Sanford Discover Sanford – Things to See & Do Sanford Demographics Events Public Art Downtown Parking Map Free Trolley Service Marina & Marina Day Slips Museum How Do I Apply For Job Opportunities Building Permit Certificate of Appropriateness Special Event Permit Find My City Commission District Vacant and Foreclosed Property Registration Downtown Sanford Parking Pay Utility Bill Parking Ticket Report Non-Emergency Incident Code Violation Criminal Activity Request Public Record Pavilion or Facility Rental Utility Service Recycle Bin Submit General Service Requests Police Records Request Contact Us Water & Sewer Utilities Home Government Public Works & Utilities Water & Sewer Utilities Utility News and Projects Solid Waste Rate Increase Notification Annual Water Reports Water Quality 2026 Water Quality 2025 Water Quality 2024 Water Quality 2023 Water Quality 2022 Water Quality 2021 Water Quality 2020 Lead Safe Community Water Quality 1,4 _Dioxane Vacuum Sewer Check for Service Availability in your Area by filling out the Utility Availability Connection Cost Request Form. Pay My Bill The City offers several convenient options to pay your utility bill Click Here Set Up Utility Service Set up Residential or Commercial Utility billing Get Started Forms & Publications Download Water and Sewer Utilities Division forms and publications Learn More Water Quality Alerts and Notifications View Current Water & Sewer Utilities Establish Utility Service Bill Payment Pretreatment Water Conservation Unidirectional Flushing Program (UDF) Water Meter Replacement Program 2025 Water Quality Report 2024 Water Quality Report 2023 Water Quality Report 2021 Water Quality Report 2020 Water Quality Report Sanford Utility Manual Application for Residential Water Service Application for Commercial Water Service Application for Discontinuation of Utilities Application for Reclaimed Water Service Service Line Warranty Did You Wonder When you pay your Utility bill, where does the money go? Find Out More Elizabeth Dwyer (407) 688.5102 Email: Customer Service Supervisor Michael Cannon (407) 688.5177 Email: Utilities Engineering Manager After 4pm for Emergency Utility Assistance** 407.688.5100 Email: After Hours Service **This Email is not reviewed till after 4pm – for afterhours assistance ONLY. 01 Nov 49th Annual Golden Age Games The City of Sanford Water, Wastewater and Reclaimed Water Management System Service Areas include land within the City of Sanford and unincorporated portions of Seminole County. The City of Sanford Utility System serves the City’s residential, commercial, light industrial, agricultural, and rural areas. The Utility Department also has the Customer Service Division for all Utility functions from meter reading, billing, payment receipts, billing questions, and public education for water conservation. Christmas Holiday In observance of the Christmas holiday, City Hall will be CLOSED from Wednesday, December 24th through Friday, December 26th. We will resume normal business hours on Monday, December 29th, 2025. This closure includes the Utility Department main office. If you have an emergency, please contact the after-hours line at 407-688-5100 &times; 2022 Water Quality Report Set Up Utility Service Set up Residential or Commercial Utility billing Get Started Pay My Bill The City offers several convenient options to pay your utility bill Click Here Forms & Publications Download Water and Sewer Utilities Division forms and publications Learn More Utility Department Frequently Asked Questions What do I do if my water bill is too high? If you have an unusually high bill, please contact the City of Sanford Utilities at 407.688.5100 or email at utilitycustomerservice@sanfordfl.gov and request a Re-Read work order right away. The customer is still responsible in making a payment until the matter is resolved. Who reads my water meter? The City of Sanford&nbsp; &nbsp;started the replacement of our previous AMR drive by meter system to an &nbsp;Advanced Metering Infrastructure (AMI) system in 2024.&nbsp; AMI is an integrated system of water meters, communications networks, and data management systems that enables the city to provide enhanced customer service for its utility customers. Advanced metering technology allows the city to read water meters remotely and collect water usage hourly from the office. AMI operates with the latest technology currently available to provide more precise consumption data, ensure accurate readings and customer billings.&nbsp; Customers can sign-up to our customer water meter portal to gain access to the same hourly water usage and set-up/manage water consumption alerts on their account(s). For instruction on how to sign-up up to the water meter portal, click the Bill Payment item to the left of this paragraph. For additional information call Utility Customer Service at 407.688.5100. What is a boil water notice? The City is required to implement a boil water notice upon a water break, or if the system pressure goes below 20 PSI. The City samples the water, samples are sent to a laboratory, and and upon two consecutive days of good samples the boil water notice is then lifted. What do I do if I have poor water quility (i.e. taste; odor; discoloration)? Please call Customer Service at 407.688.5100 and ask for the Water Quality Engineer. The water quality issue can either be on the Customer side or City side with a number of possibilities. A work order can be generated to send City Staff to the address to investigate. What programs does the City of Sanford have if you need assistance with your water bill? To help a Sanford Neighbor with emergency assistance to pay their utility bill, the City of Sanford Utilities has “A Good Neighbor Utility Fund”. Candidates can obtain an application through customer service or online at www.sanfordfl.gov . The employees donate different items to raise funds for this program and quarterly applicants are selected, and portion of the funds that are raised gets applied towards our Sanford Residents water bill. What programs does the City of Sanford have if you need assistance with your water bill? To help a Sanford Neighbor with emergency assistance to pay their utility bill, the City of Sanford Utilities has “A Good Neighbor Utility Fund”. Candidates can obtain an application through customer service or online at www.sanfordfl.gov . The employees donate different items to raise funds for this program and quarterly applicants are selected, and portion of the funds that are raised gets applied towards our Sanford Residents water bill. What do I do if my water bill is too high? If you have an unusually high bill, please contact the City of Sanford Utilities at 407.688.5100 or email at utilitycustomerservice@sanfordfl.gov and request a Re-Read work order right away. The customer is still responsible in making a payment until the matter is resolved. Who reads my water meter? The City of Sanford replaced our previous AMR drive by meter system to A MI Advanced Metering Infrastructure system in 2024. The City gets reads by satellite each month utilizing Advanced Metering Infrastructure (AMI) Technology. The City is no longer using drive by method to get meter reads by driving at a slow pace while the reading equipment automatically collects the meter readings. With AMI, the reader does not have to read the meters in any route order or physically visit the meter to read them. Advanced Metering Infrastructure (AMI) is an integrated system of water meters, communications networks, and data management systems that enables the City to provide enhanced customer service for its utility customers. Advanced metering technology will allow the City to read water meters remotely and collect water usage data daily from the office! Each meter is read between 28 and 35 days in the customer’s billing cycle. AMI meters will operate with the latest technology currently available to provide more precise consumption data, ensure accurate readings and enable billing through antenna and satellite systems. For more information call Utility Customer Service at 407.688.5100. What is a boil water notice? The City is required to implement a boil water notice upon a water break, or if the system pressure goes below 20 PSI. The City samples the water, samples are sent to a laboratory, and and upon two consecutive days of good samples the boil water notice is then lifted. What do I do if I have poor water quility (i.e. taste; odor; discoloration)? Please call Customer Service at 407.688.5100 and ask for the Water Quality Engineer. The water quality issue can either be on the Customer side or City side with a number of possibilities. A work order can be generated to send City Staff to the address to investigate. What programs does the City of Sanford have if you need assistance with your water bill? To help a Sanford Neighbor with emergency assistance to pay their utility bill, the City of Sanford Utilities has “A Good Neighbor Utility Fund”. Candidates can obtain an application through customer service or online at www.sanfordfl.gov . The employees donate different items to raise funds for this program and quarterly applicants are selected, and portion of the funds that are raised gets applied towards our Sanford Residents water bill. What do I do if my water bill is too high? If you have an unusually high bill, please contact the City of Sanford Utilities at 407.688.5100 or email at utilitycustomerservice@sanfordfl.gov and request a Re-Read work order right away. The customer is still responsible in making a payment until the matter is resolved. Who reads my water meter? The City of Sanford began the replacement of our previous AMR drive by meter system to an&nbsp;Advanced Metering Infrastructure (AMI) system in 2024. The city is no longer using a drive by method to get meter reads by driving at a slow pace while the reading equipment automatically collects the meter readings. AMI is an integrated system of water meters, communications networks, and data management systems that enables the city to provide enhanced customer service for its utility customers. AMI allows the city to read water meters remotely and collect water usage data hourly from the office.&nbsp; AMI meters operate with the latest technology currently available to provide more precise consumption data, ensure accurate readings and customer billings. Customers can sign-up for our customer meter portal to access this same hourly water usage and to set and manager alerts on their accounts. For instructions for signing up to the customer meter portal, click on the Bill Payment link to the left of this paragraph. Or for more information call Utility Customer Service at 407.688.5100. What is a boil water notice? The City is required to implement a boil water notice upon a water break, or if the system pressure goes below 20 PSI. The City samples the water, samples are sent to a laboratory, and and upon two consecutive days of good samples the boil water notice is then lifted. What do I do if I have poor water quility (i.e. taste; odor; discoloration)? Please call Customer Service at 407.688.5100 and ask for the Water Quality Engineer. The water quality issue can either be on the Customer side or City side with a number of possibilities. A work order can be generated to send City Staff to the address to investigate. What programs does the City of Sanford have if you need assistance with your water bill? To help a Sanford Neighbor with emergency assistance to pay their utility bill, the City of Sanford Utilities has “A Good Neighbor Utility Fund”. Candidates can obtain an application through customer service or online at www.sanfordfl.gov . The employees donate different items to raise funds for this program and quarterly applicants are selected, and portion of the funds that are raised gets applied towards our Sanford Residents water bill. Good Neighbor Utility Fund Learn More Utilities 101 - An Informative Video on all Things Utilities Walk and Talk with Brynt Johnson - Reclaimed Water 101 Home Jobs Online Payments Contact Us Employee Email Accessibility Connect With Us facebook-square instagram youtube home linkedin twitter 300 N Park Ave Sanford FL, 32771 Opening Hours: Mon – Thur: 7:00 am – 5:30 pm Fri: 8:00 am – 1:00 pm Most Requested Events Calendar Special Event Application Rental Opportunities Water S